# Rebuild and launch

After you finish a task the user gave you, rebuild the desktop program and launch it before the final reply.

Use the debug executable with the interface packed inside it. Do not start `npm run tauri dev` and do not leave the window loading `localhost`.

On this computer the Rust output goes to `D:\HealthEngine-build\cargo-target`. Stop a running `health-engine.exe` before the link step so the file can be replaced, then start the new one:

```powershell
$env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR = "D:\HealthEngine-build\cargo-target"
$env:TEMP = "D:\HealthEngine-build\tmp"
$env:TMP = "D:\HealthEngine-build\tmp"
$env:CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG = "line-tables-only"
Get-Process health-engine -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force
npm run build
cargo build --manifest-path src-tauri\Cargo.toml
Start-Process "D:\HealthEngine-build\cargo-target\debug\health-engine.exe"
```

Confirm the Health Engine window opened and is not the “localhost refused to connect” page. Say the executable path in the reply.
